From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] debian: Name one Maintainer, list the other in Uploaders

Maintainer must hold exactly one name and address (Debian Policy 5.6.2);
co-maintainers go in Uploaders. Current dpkg enforces this, so on Ubuntu
26.10 (and Debian testing) the package doesn't build at all:

  dpkg-source: error: cannot parse Maintainer field value "Izzie Walton
  <izzie@iwalton.com>, Joshua Boniface <joshua@boniface.me>"

Found building the .deb for arm64, which Jellyfin doesn't publish.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 debian/control | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debian/control b/debian/control
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 Source: jellyfin-desktop
 Section: video
 Priority: optional
-Maintainer:  Izzie Walton <izzie@iwalton.com>, Joshua Boniface <joshua@boniface.me>
+Maintainer: Izzie Walton <izzie@iwalton.com>
+Uploaders: Joshua Boniface <joshua@boniface.me>
 Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 10),
                autoconf,
                automake,
-- 
